    [Refactor][KVPP] Remove Model Runner V1 support (#18958)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Simplify KVPP code outside the V1 runner ahead of its removal: use the
    V2 speculator API for draft-cache ownership, remove shared-test V1
    parameterizations, and let KVPP E2E cases use the default runner. Update
    KVPP source documentation across the user guide, configuration
    reference, design document, general support table, and PP guide:
    document eager and PIECEWISE execution, supported connector
    integrations, and model/speculation constraints consistently. Remove
    runner-version distinctions and preserve the execution settings of
    historical benchmark data. Generated .po translations are unchanged.
    
    Keep the V1 runner, its tests, and the cache-binding compatibility
    interface unchanged; they can be removed together with the V1 execution
    path. No additional runner-version rejection is introduced.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No new options or explicit runner-version validation.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Python AST parsing and git diff whitespace checks passed for the
    updates.
    - Checked changed Markdown fences, relative file links, and the JSON in
    all 3 launch examples. Verified the PR has no .po diffs.
    - Cross-checked graph restrictions against KVPPConfig.validate and
    TestKVPPConfig.test_graph_modes; connector/model constraints against the
    configuration validator and cache-placement implementation.
    - Removed the redundant V1 rejection test along with its guard.
    - Verified V1 runner source is unchanged from the rebase target.
    - Local format checks could not run because pre-commit is unavailable.
    NPU validation remains subject to CI.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
